speechtext:
That this House call upon the government to commit itself, on the week of the second annual Rural Revitalization Day and the anniversary of the birth of Agnes MacPhail, the first woman elected to this House and an untiring champion of the rights of rural Canadians, to provide for a vital economic, social and environmentally sustainable future for rural Canada and the millions of Canadians who live in our vast rural areas, by implementing a program to:
1)	stabilize family farm incomes and ease the crippling debt load which at present threatens the very survival of tens of thousands of family farms;
2)	assist fishing communities to survive the current crisis in the fishery and take steps to ensure the proper management of the fishery in the future;
3)	modify existing transportation and other infrastructure policies to assure all primary producers, co-operative and rural small businesses that they can be competitive in both the domestic and the international market-place;
4)	provide a full range of education, health and other social policies to enable young families, the elderly and others to live comfortably in rural and isolated parts of Canada; and
5)	provide a full range of services, including shelters, child care services and skills training to support the crucial role played by women in all rural communities.
March 23, 1990

a)	The Hon. George Hees
He was appointed by Order in Council as Ambassador-at-large and Prime Minister's Personal Representative;
(i)	his conditions of employment are those prescribed for senior officials appointed on a full-time basis by Order in Council;
(ii)	his salary is in the range $101,400-$123,400;
(iii)	his employment is indeterminate.
b)	Mr. Allan Gotlieb
He is currently part-time Chairman of the Canada Council, appointed by Order in Council;

The House resumed consideration of the motion of Mr. Hovdebo:
